3	// The subject of the printer panel's conversation: what the model is told and
4	// may call there, and the picture cards the page draws in the thread.
5	//
6	// The conversation is the whole panel. The model does the understanding --
7	// which printer someone has, what changed on one they own, how to reach it --
8	// and acts through the session's tools, which check its decision against the
9	// printer data and carry it out. The person's yes in the conversation is the
10	// confirmation; the one card is printer_connect's, where a credential is typed
11	// so it never passes through the model.
12	//
13	// A session is opened for one printer question -- add a printer, change this
14	// one, connect this one -- and is discarded when the panel closes. Nothing
15	// here is written to the project: AgentHost keeps the thread in an in-memory
16	// document, and printers are saved through IPrinterBackend, which owns the
17	// only route to Orca.
